   "text": "These documents follow one argument from diagnosis to decision: officers in China described Nationalist corruption from 1943, the Ambassador proposed in 1947 to meter aid against it, and in November 1948 the Secretary of State listed corrupt officials among the reasons the United States would not undertake all-out aid. The 1950 Philippine instruction shows the same reasoning turned into conditions on further aid."
