   "kind": "heading",
   "text": "5. Bribery of the U.S. Congress and the Korean troop withdrawal (1978)",
   "level": 1
  },
  {
   "kind": "prose",
   "text": "The Tongsun Park affair, in which South Korean figures were accused of bribing members of Congress, appears in the 1978 papers as a reason to postpone the first combat troop withdrawal from Korea: the scandal, not the withdrawal itself, set the limits of what Congress would vote."
  },
  {
   "kind": "document",
   "volumeId": "frus1977-80v13",
   "documentId": "d84",
   "notes": [
    "Agent finding, run s9, 2026-10-30: The NSC staff paper argues for postponing the first withdrawals because Congress cannot address Korean security while the Tongsun Park affair hangs over it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "excerpt",
   "volumeId": "frus1977-80v13",
   "documentId": "d84",
   "text": "Postponement of the first withdrawals—on grounds that the Congress cannot be expected to address the security dimensions of the problem while the Tongsun Park affair hangs over them—would remove a contentious issue from the Executive-Legislative agenda."
  },
  {
   "kind": "document",
   "volumeId": "frus1977-80v13",
   "documentId": "d92",
   "notes": [
    "Agent finding, run s9, 2026-10-30: The interagency options memorandum carries the same justification into Option 2, postponing the December 1978 brigade withdrawal."
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "document",
   "volumeId": "frus1977-80v13",
   "documentId": "d94",
   "notes": [
    "Agent finding, run s9, 2026-10-30: At the White House meeting Holbrooke says the issue is the Tongsun Park affair, not the withdrawal, and that Congressmen fear voting any aid to Korea."
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "excerpt",
   "volumeId": "frus1977-80v13",
   "documentId": "d94",
   "text": "The issue is not the withdrawal but the Tongsun Park affair. Because of “Koreagate,” Congressmen fear political retribution at the polls if they vote for any sort of aid to Korea this year."
  },
